<.shell title="QR scanner" current={:qr_scanner}>
  <h1>QR scanner</h1>
  <p class="lead">Scan ID cards with the phone's camera.</p>

  <div class="example measure">
    <.qr_scanner id="sample-scanner" label="Scan ID cards" variant={:success} />
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A page used on a phone to read QR codes, such as checking an ID card or taking attendance at the door.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>One big button starts the camera. The picture fills the width while it scans.</li>
    <li>Stop scanning puts the button back.</li>
    <li>
      The Sound switch is a <a href={page_path(:forms) <> "#switch"}>compact switch</a>
      under the button. The phone remembers it.
    </li>
    <li>Each read goes to the page, which answers with a <a href={page_path(:band)}>band</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.qr_scanner label="Scan ID cards" /&gt;</code>. The page handles <code>"scanned"</code>.
    <code>data-continuous</code>
    keeps scanning after a read.
  </p>
</.shell>
